 - [ ] N2 Shaft successful stale bytes: Return/reentry, late success cannot corrupt the new epoch/camera/resource census.
 - [ ] N3 Shaft real WebGL context loss: exit once, dispose once, restore/focus.
 - [ ] N4 Shaft manually paused hidden/visible round trip remains paused.
+
+## Readiness status (2026-10-06, producer)
+
+Harness corrected after preview-run-1 (historical failed run preserved in
+runtime/shaft/preview-run-1): exact-float seek now uses transient step=any with
+the native value setter plus real input/change events; S2 implements the October 6
+retained-partial-stock contract (telemetry counts vs live progression uniforms,
+wholly-return no-advance/no-engagement, per-gain counted-engagement causality,
+previous-pass depth ahead of the cutter leading face); restore snapshots are
+compared settled-to-settled at one consistent post-render phase with numeric
+tolerance for recomputed camera matrices; focus identity uses the stored trigger
+element reference; N2 counts the shaft root manufacturing-study-root; N3
+instruments the study-root removal and one owned geometry disposal plus zeroed
+owned-resource counters instead of the legacy ring disposed counter; S1 accepts
+exactly one manufacturing-core-{full,lite}.glb request because the adaptive
+quality ladder legitimately serves either bundle per session (preview-run-1 got
+full, diagnostic-run-1 desktop got lite on the same dist); the slow-exit camera
+check is per-time paused stability and cross-window drift is report-only
+(authored anchors blend 7.2 to 9.7).
+
+Diagnostic run (harness validation, current preview build):
+runtime/shaft/diagnostic-run-1 - S3 S4 S5 S6 N1 N2 N4 pass on both viewports;
+S1 failed only the tier-conditional bundle expectation (fixed above); S2 uniform
+capture now waits for a visible shaping beat (fixed above); S7 desktop showed ULP
+noise (fixed above) plus one unsettled exploded-Return baseline (fixed above);
+S8 fails only poster static entry, a real app defect below. No gates are checked
+yet: two agreeing complete runs against the rebuilt preview are still required.
+
+App defects found (for parent; outside producer ownership):
+
+1. Poster-tier shaft entry throws before any dialog:
+   "Error: The shaft inspection is not available yet" at
+   src/scene/inspection/story.ts:44 via enterInspection
+   (src/state/inspectionStore.ts:118) from the entry button
+   (src/components/RingInspection.tsx:155). The shaft descriptor is registered
+   at module scope of src/scene/inspection/InspectionScene.tsx:16, which never
+   loads when the canvas bundle is absent (poster tier), so the static shaft
+   study is unreachable. Reduced-motion static passes; only the poster path is
+   broken.
